.TH PARAMTRACKS 2
.SH NAME
paramtracks: new, cmd, hit, draw, value \- a labelled parameter-slider control band
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "draw.m";
include "paramtracks.m";
paramtracks := load Paramtracks Paramtracks->PATH;
Tracks: import paramtracks;

t := paramtracks->new(image, font);
t.cmd("colour foreground 16r20272cff\encolour accent 16rb85c38ff\en" +
      "band 74\entrack sigma 0 25 colour accent\enset sigma 10");
t.draw(image.r);
(name, value, ok) := t.hit(pointer.xy, image.r);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Paramtracks
is a small Tk/Plot-style command language for the labelled band of
parameter sliders several danby models draw along one edge of their
window: equal-width horizontal slots, one per live parameter, hit-
tested by fraction-across-the-slot and drawn as a line, a dot at the
current value, and a
.RI \(lq name " " value \(rq
label underneath.  It replaces what several models used to hand-roll
independently (band-hit-test arithmetic and slider drawing, duplicated
near-verbatim save for the parameter names, ranges, and pixel
constants) with one reusable module, the same way
.IR plot (2)
replaced per-model chart-drawing code.
.PP
.B Cmd
accepts newline-separated commands:
.TP
.BI "colour " name " " rgba
Defines a named colour, resolved via the track image's font's display.
.TP
.BI "band " height
Sets the control band's pixel height (the bottom
.I height
pixels of whatever rect
.B draw
/
.B hit
are given).
.TP
.BI "track " name " " lo " " hi " [colour " colourname "]"
Adds (or reconfigures) a track; its value defaults to
.IR lo .
.TP
.BI "set " name " " value
Sets a track's current value directly, e.g. after model init or reset.
.PP
.B Draw
renders the band within the bottom
.B band
pixels of
.IR r .
.B Hit
tests a pointer position against
.IR r 's
band: if it falls inside, the hit track's value is updated from the
pointer's fractional position across its slot (clamped to
.RI [0.01,\ 0.99] )
and
.RI ( name ", " value ", 1)"
is returned; otherwise
.RI (\(lq\(rq,\ 0.0,\ 0).
.B Value
reads a named track's current value without going through
.BR hit .
.SH SOURCE
.B /module/paramtracks.m
.br
.B /appl/lib/paramtracks.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR plot (2),
.IR danby (1)
